From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: spi: mediatek,spi-mt65xx: add MT6897

The SPI controllers of the MediaTek MT6897 (Dimensity 8300) SoC are of the
IPM design that MT6991 has. The MediaTek driver in the OnePlus MT6897
kernel matches them with its mt6985 data: pad selection, the enhanced
timing registers, 36-bit DMA addresses and the IPM register layout, which
are the features of the mainline mt6991 data. Add MT6897 with
mediatek,mt6991-spi as the fallback.

The MediaTek driver also has a quad mode and switches the chip select by
software; the mainline driver uses neither, as on MT6991.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/mediatek,spi-mt65xx.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/mediatek,spi-mt65xx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/mediatek,spi-mt65xx.yaml
index 3bf3eb1..2a746b4 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/mediatek,spi-mt65xx.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/spi/mediatek,spi-mt65xx.yaml
@@ -41,6 +41,7 @@ properties:
           - const: mediatek,spi-ipm
       - items:
           - enum:
+              - mediatek,mt6897-spi
               - mediatek,mt8196-spi
           - const: mediatek,mt6991-spi
       - items:
